       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum for IR.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **500 mg PO twice or three times daily.** This is a typical starting or titration dose.\n\nTell me the dose and formulation (IR or XR) you want, and I'll enter it right away."
